Brick is a fork of the upstream project as of mid-2026 (after the v0.3.0
release). The Go router now lives under apps/router/src/spatial-router, and
the retained CPU inference binding under apps/router/candle-binding.
Unused ML/NLP bindings and generic router subsystems were removed. Go module paths and crate names were rebranded
(e.g. github.com/vllm-project/semantic-router/src/semantic-router ->
github.com/regolo-ai/brick-SR1/apps/router/src/spatial-router;
candle-semantic-router -> candle-spatial-router), runtime branding was changed
to Brick/Regolo, and additional components were added on top (CLI, economics,
sticky routing, multimodal gateway). Modified files carry notices as required
by Section 4(b) of the Apache License; this notice preserves upstream
attribution separately from product identity.
